  log: {
    title: "Monitor: Log",
    body: [
      "The daemon's log on the node this page is acting on (use the **Node** menu to pick another member, **Cluster** for every node's, or a **Gateway** for the nodes that serve it). It is the same text that goes to the system journal, and it is also kept in a file in the state directory (`dnsdir.log`, rotated at 100 MB with the two previous files kept), so it survives a restart.",
      ["h", "What you can do here"],
      ["ul", ["Search the log for a word, an address or a name.", "Show only warnings and errors.", "Follow the log live.", "Download what you see, or a full **tshoot** bundle for support."]],
      ["h", "Step by step: find what happened to one server"],
      ["ol", ["Type the address in **Filter text**, for example `10.0.0.5 DOWN`. A line must contain every word.", "Choose a **Time range** and, if you like, a **Level**.", "Tick **Live** to follow new lines as they arrive."]],
      ["h", "Finding things"],
      ["ul", ["**Filter** takes words; a line must contain every one of them (any case); join words with `OR` to accept either, for example `error OR warn` (AND binds first). For example `10.0.0.5 DOWN` or `domain google.com`.", "**Level** keeps lines at that level and above. Debug lines exist only while the daemon's log level is *debug* (Configure ▸ General).", "**Time range** and **lines** bound the answer; the status line under the list says when older lines were cut.", "**Live** refreshes every few seconds and follows the newest line while you are at the bottom; scroll up to read and it stops following. **Download** saves what is shown as a text file.", "**Cluster** or a **Gateway**: each node's log is asked with the same filters and the lines are merged by time, with the node after the time (and at the start of each line in the download). **Lines** is the most for all of them together. The lines are not split by gateway: a gateway's log is the whole log of the nodes that serve it. A node that does not answer is named in red under the list."]],
      ["h", "tshoot"],
      "**tshoot** downloads one .tgz with everything that helps to find out why something does not work, from **every node** of the cluster (the node you are signed in to asks the others, whichever node the Node menu has picked): each node's log (the newest 20000 lines), configuration and its saved versions, cluster view, gateway, DNS-pool, BGP, anycast, virtual-MAC-test and update state, host numbers for the last hour, the addresses, links, routes (every table), rules, neighbors, ARP, listening sockets, the sysctl settings that matter to ARP and routing, the firewall rules, FRR's BGP and BFD output and configuration, service status, the system journal of AnyName, the kernel log tail and the system's version and load. It always includes 8 seconds of ARP and neighbor-discovery traffic on each gateway interface and a dump of every goroutine of the daemon (what it is busy with, for a node that is up but stuck). Passwords, the gateway key, tokens, join codes and private keys are removed before anything is written, command lines of other programs are not included, and each node's README.txt lists the files and says what could not be collected. A node that cannot be reached has a note instead of a folder. Nothing is changed on any node.",
      ["h", "What is logged"],
      "Server up and down changes, domains that start or stop answering on a server (so a single failing domain shows even while the server stays up), gateway start-up and hand-over, a node's CPU, memory or fullest disk going over 85% (a warning, naming what is over; this node and every cluster member) and the line when it is back at 85% or below, configuration changes (each one says what was enabled, disabled, paused or resumed), updates (including auto-update turned on or off), BGP and web sign-in events.",
      ["h", "Fields"],
      ["fields", [["Filter text", "Words, separated by spaces. A line is shown only if it contains every one, in any case. Applied as you type."], ["Level", "All levels, Info and above, Warnings and errors, or Errors only. Default all."], ["Time range", "The buttons **Last hour**, **Last day** and **Last week** choose how much history the graphs show. They are per window; the history kept is 7 days."], ["Lines", "The most lines shown: 200, 1000 (default) or 5000, newest kept."], ["Live", "Ticked (the default): the list refreshes every few seconds and follows the newest line while you are at the bottom."]]],
      ["cli", "dnsdir --tshoot --all-nodes   (the tshoot bundle of every node, written to dnsdir-tshoot-HOST-TIME.tgz; without --all-nodes just this node; --tshoot-file F.tgz names the file; the ARP / neighbor-discovery capture is always taken)\nkill -USR1 $(pidof dnsdir)   (writes every goroutine's stack to the journal: journalctl -u dnsdir; for a daemon that is up but not answering)\ndnsdir --log\ndnsdir --log --log-min warn --log-since 6h\ndnsdir --log --log-grep \"server 192.0.2.53\" --log-lines 200\n(without --log-lines the whole matching log is printed; redirect it to a file to keep it)"],
    ],
  },
